e coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124576 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6641b2cf-00bc-5542-a566-5b8689f2f2a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Images of the Basis Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203ae31f-e7d7-5ba9-985d-c5c53968ef9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392247} {:answer/id #uuid "d9505477-b80c-5e60-9ad5-b8cceaf69da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392248} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7cd5bf-81b1-5350-b65a-736745d05714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392249} {:answer/id #uuid "4e43d5b8-d929-5ed6-8f43-093ad3710dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392250} {:answer/id #uuid "c1643dd1-1ac2-5766-b8de-dea684f1a01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc7cd5bf-81b1-5350-b65a-736745d05714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392249} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ac46a3d-440c-54c6-a48d-2372df405d0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "217d7c6a-01fa-5c09-8fc9-462942a415a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-38884" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}\\,$ if $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}\\,$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124541 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22ca4f81-6fec-5822-b281-5ce1e23d399e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis in a Three-Dimensional Vector Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa4e200d-3059-501b-ab48-6218a57adb56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366092} {:answer/id #uuid "07fc866b-fe6c-5b59-a12b-1c07c6f776d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366093} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e63e01-ec4a-57a5-86b7-843609011e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366094} {:answer/id #uuid "32c297e8-07e1-5fab-ad4c-57169fea2237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366095} {:answer/id #uuid "5466569e-0352-5327-9298-ff146556b7cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5466569e-0352-5327-9298-ff146556b7cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366096} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b50d6d-f46c-5fab-8128-2948e6ef2591" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366091}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c06910f-cdf8-5abe-b301-896973ca0101" :question/math-academy-id "q-38919" :question/problem "The basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the matrix $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$ of the linear transformation $T:{R}^{3}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}a & 1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & b & -5 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{1}{5} & c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $\\,a+b+c,\\,$ given that  \n\n$$\nT([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}x+y+z \\\\ x-y \\\\ x-z\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1},$ ${b}_{2},$ and ${b}_{3}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3}) & =T([\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}])=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2}),$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {b}_{3} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) & T({b}_{3}) \\\\ | & | & | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & -3 & -1 & -10\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{1}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{1}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=3,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-2$ and \n\n$$\na+b+c=3+(-2)+(-2)=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124540 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "823a7d28-5a92-5901-8ee0-e5116df6766b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Image of a Vector Given the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00eb9f24-6f46-54fd-881a-8d0acb355862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 